FUN_0000_e584 intro animation-SCRIPT interpreter (frame loop): STRSEG base-loss + dropped 38bc CF.

Patch 071 reconstructed only e584's header (up to the FUN_1000_38cc frame-sync).  The frame loop after it
walks the intro animation script -- a table of 6-byte records at ES:[b6ec] where ES = STRSEG = the far
resource segment word[DGROUP:0x70] (0x2d74).  Ghidra dropped ES=STRSEG (so *b6ec and the key-event record
deref bare offsets -> SIGSEGV at build/fist.c:33951), pointer-scaled the cursor advance (uint* +3 = +12
bytes vs the asm's +6), and dropped FUN_1000_38bc's carry (rendering its key-record read as always-taken via
a hardcoded bVar11=false, which then deref'd a stale far pointer).  Reconstruct faithfully per asm
0xe60b..0xe6db: base the record reads at g_mem+(STRSEG<<4), advance b6ec by 6 bytes, and gate the key-event
block on the frame-poll carry g_fist_cf (threaded through FUN_1000_35a7 / FUN_1000_38bc, patches 073/074).

Each frame command is posted to the intro TASK via FUN_0000_e2c2 (which writes EBX -> task+0x3f2, sets the
extender service selector aa10 = 0x64, and calls the extender gate FUN_0000_e339).  The extender gate
currently no-ops task-control ops while task[0]==0, so the intro frames are POSTED but not yet rendered --
the actual per-frame render is the extender TASK-EXECUTION service (op 0x64), the next frontier to pixels.
With this patch the intro loop no longer crashes: it posts its frame commands and advances (the empty-queue
poll returns CF=1, so 38bc returns at once and the frame-delay spin is INT-8-tick bounded), letting e584
run to completion and execution proceed past the intro.
